        "Content": "Period residence dating from c. 1843.\r\nAdjoining former church dating from c. 1845.\r\nOccupying an impressive c. 1.75-acre riverside site in the centre of Portlaw.\r\nThe house extends to approximately 175 sq. m. (1,884 sq. ft)\r\nPresented in excellent condition throughout.\r\nRetains a wealth of original period features.\r\nEnhanced by a range of modern upgrades.\r\nSignificant redevelopment or alternative use potential (subject to planning permission).\r\nMature landscaped grounds offering privacy and seclusion.\r\nClodagh River forms the property's northern boundary.\r\nRare opportunity to acquire a unique property with character and charm.\r\nExtensive grounds with substantial future development potential.\r\nAvailable with vacant possession upon completion of the sale.\r\n\r\nThe Manse is a charming period residence dating from circa 1843, occupying an impressive c. 1.75-acre riverside site in the centre of Portlaw. The property is presented in excellent condition and retains a wealth of original features, complemented by modern upgrades throughout. A standout feature is the adjoining former church, dating from circa 1845, which offers exceptional potential for redevelopment or alternative use, subject to planning. Set amidst mature landscaped grounds with the Clodagh River forming its northern boundary, The Manse presents a rare opportunity to acquire a unique property combining character, privacy, extensive grounds and significant future potential. The property will be available with vacant possession upon close of sale. Total floor area extending to approximately 175 sq. m (1,884 sq. ft) \r\n\r\nAvailable with vacant possession upon completion of the sale."
